Let $0\le r\le n$ and let $K\le S_n$ be the Young subgroup of the two-block set partition $\{0,\dots,n-r-1\}\cup\{n-r,\dots,n-1\}$ of the underlying set ([[def-finite-symmetric-group-and-permutation-notation]], [[def-young-subgroup-tabloid-and-permutation-module]]); thus $K$ is the image of the external direct product $S_{n-r}	imes S_r$ acting on the two blocks ([[def-external-direct-product-of-groups]]). Identify the complex character ring $R(K)$ with $R(S_{n-r})\otimes_{\mathbb Z}R(S_r)$ by external tensor products $\chi oxtimes\psi$ of characters ([[def-tensor-product-of-complex-representations]], [[lem-character-ring-of-a-direct-product-is-the-tensor-product]]). Then for every $\lambda\vdash n$, in $R(K)$,
$$
\chi^\lambda ig|_{K}=\sum_{
u\vdash n-r}\ \sum_{\mu\vdash r}c^\lambda_{
u\mu}\,\chi^
u oxtimes\chi^\mu,
$$
where $c^\lambda_{
u\mu}$ is the Littlewood–Richardson coefficient ([[def-littlewood-richardson-tableau-and-coefficient]]). In particular the multiplicity of the irreducible character $\chi^
u oxtimes\chi^\mu$ in the restricted character $\chi^\lambda|_K$ equals $c^\lambda_{
u\mu}$; for $r=n$ this says that the multiplicity is $1$ if $\mu=\lambda$ and $0$ otherwise. No choice principle is used.

The partition $\lambda=(5,4,4)$ of $13$ has hook lengths, read row by row, $7,6,5,4,1$; $5,4,3,2$; $4,3,2,1$, so its removable border strips have sizes $\{1,2,3,4,5,6,7\}$ and there is no removable strip of size $8,9,10,11,12$ or $13$ ([[lem-hooks-correspond-to-removable-border-strips]]). The Murnaghan–Nakayama rule ([[thm-murnaghan-nakayama-character-rule]]) gives:

1. $\chi^{(5,4,4)}=-1$ on the class of cycle type $(5,4,3,1)$ of $S_{13}$: the two legal removals of a $5$-strip have signs $+$ and $-$, and the recursion yields $\chi^{(3,3,2)}(4,3,1)-\chi^{(5,3)}(4,3,1)=0-1=-1$;
2. $\chi^{(5,4,4)}=2$ on the class of cycle type $(7,3,3)$: the unique legal removal of a $7$-strip has sign $+$ and yields $\chi^{(3,3)}(3,3)=1-(-1)=2$;
3. $\chi^{(5,4,4)}=0$ on every class whose cycle type contains a part in $\{8,9,10,11,12,13\}$, since $\lambda$ has no removable border strip of those sizes ([[cor-no-removable-cycle-length-strip-forces-a-character-zero]]).
